{
  "mn80:0.1": "Middle Discourses 80 ",
  "mn80:0.2": "With Vekhanasa ",
  "mn80:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn80:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn80:2.1": "Then the wanderer Vekhanasa went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "mn80:2.2": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he stood to one side, ",
  "mn80:2.3": "and expressed this heartfelt sentiment in the Buddha’s presence: ",
  "mn80:2.4": "“This is the ultimate splendor, this is the ultimate splendor.” ",
  "mn80:2.5": "“But Kaccāna, why do you say: ",
  "mn80:2.6": "‘This is the ultimate splendor, this is the ultimate splendor.’ ",
  "mn80:2.7": "What is that ultimate splendor?” ",
  "mn80:2.8": "“Worthy Gotama, the ultimate splendor is the splendor compared to which no other splendor is finer.” ",
  "mn80:2.9": "“But what is that ultimate splendor compared to which no other splendor is finer?” ",
  "mn80:2.10": "“Worthy Gotama, the ultimate splendor is the splendor compared to which no other splendor is finer.” ",
  "mn80:3.1": "“Kaccāna, you could draw this out for a long time. ",
  "mn80:3.2": "You say, ‘The ultimate splendor is the splendor compared to which no other splendor is finer.’ But you don’t describe that splendor. ",
  "mn80:3.3": "Suppose a man was to say, ",
  "mn80:3.4": "‘Whoever the finest lady in the land is, it is her that I want, her I desire!’ ",
